<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!-- The platform's shared database resilience: patience where a connection is opened
         (`PatientPgDriver`), one bounded retry for work that must survive a postgres cutover
         (`DbRetry`), and nothing else.

         AS THIN AS qits-arch-rules, and for the same two reasons. It carries no CDI bean, so it
         needs no quarkus-arc and no jandex index — both classes are reachable without a request
         context, which is what lets a background worker call them. And it does not depend on
         hibernate-core: the JDK's own `java.sql` exceptions are matched by type, and Hibernate's
         `JDBCConnectionException` BY FULLY-QUALIFIED NAME, so a consumer's ORM and this module's
         version stay uncoupled and a bare clone builds with no platform registry.

         The price is qits-arch-rules': a rename in Hibernate silently un-matches. The test sources
         carry a mirror of the type for that reason — the drift surfaces there first.

         Two dependencies. jboss-logging, the logging API every Quarkus application already holds —
         a retry that says nothing is a service that goes quiet for fifteen seconds with no record
         of why. And pgjdbc in PROVIDED scope, which the driver delegates to and which every
         consumer already ships; see the dependency's own note. -->
    <parent>
        <groupId>eu.wohlben.qits</groupId>
        <artifactId>qits-integrations-quarkus</artifactId>
        <version>2026.810.184518</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>qits-db-core</artifactId>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>
    <name>qits-db-core</name>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.jboss.logging</groupId>
            <artifactId>jboss-logging</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <!-- PROVIDED, never compile: `PatientPgDriver` delegates to pgjdbc, and every consumer
                 already ships it inside quarkus-jdbc-postgresql. A compile-scope dependency here
                 would hand a second copy to every consumer of this module — including the ones that
                 only want `DbRetry` — and make this module's pgjdbc version a fleet-wide pin.
                 Provided is on the test classpath too, so the suite compiles and runs. -->
            <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>provided</scope>
        </dependency>

        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
